== Item 1/2: exhaustive enumeration over every coin sequence (ref_exact.py; block value a=1,b=2,c=4,d=8)
rule 'worded' = steps 1-4 as worded, step 4 applied to all blocks at once (condition evaluated on the array after step 3)
rule 'scan'   = same, but step 4 scans blocks in reading order and dimers placed earlier in the scan count as touching
rule 'pre'    = step 4 replaced by: fill every new block that was empty after step 1 (before the deletion of step 2)
(for non-tilings met by 'worded', step 3 was applied to every remaining dimer of a block)
brute-force numbers of tilings: {1: 2, 2: 8, 3: 64, 4: 1024, 5: 32768}
