Smallest change found: in step 4, a block emptied by step 2 must not be refilled; equivalently fill exactly the blocks
that were empty after step 1 (then the corner condition is automatic), equivalently scan in reading order counting new dimers.
Proof sketch: if new block X is empty after step 1, each of its corners is covered in the old tiling by a dimer lying in the
neighbouring new block and touching the shared corner; that dimer is either deleted (pair) or slides away from the corner. So
all four corners are free, no two such blocks are adjacent, and counting (n+1)+m of them gives exactly the free vertices/4.
Under either corrected rule: every tiling of orders 1-5 has probability exactly 2^-(n(n+1)/2); number of sequences is NOT
the number of tilings from order 3 (80, 2464, 297024 sequences for 64, 1024, 32768 tilings): tosses = n(n+1)/2 + deletions.
Exact mean deletions going from order n to n+1, n=1..5: 0, 1/4, 3/4, 97/64, 163/64.
Exact mean tosses to reach order 1..6: 1, 3, 6.25, 11, 17.515625, 26.0625

